              <td height="2">
                <div align="center"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="5" align="center"><b>Enough 
                  casting Israeli aggression as mere "retaliations"</b></font></div>
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
              <td height="2">
                <hr height="1">
              </td>
            </tr>
            <tr align="left" valign="top"> 
              <td height="304"> 
                <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><b>PMWATCH 
                  - Jan 22, 2002</b><br>
                  <br>
                  Time and again, day in and day out, without let up, and in spite 
                  of our relentless protests, AP, Reuters, Knight Ridder, CNN, 
                  NPR, and all the major media outlets, insist, as if either hypnotized 
                  or simply out of spite against elementary common sense and glaring 
                  reality, that the best way to describe Israeli actions is by 
                  using the world "retaliation" or "retaliatory".<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; 
                  </span>I have myself written dozens upon dozens of letters to 
                  newspapers, individual journalists and editors, sat down for 
                  hours with foreign desk editors and challenged them to explain 
                  why they insist on framing Israeli actions PRECISELY as official 
                  Israel wants them to be framed, that is as mere reactions, retaliations, 
                  i.e., </font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">as 
                  acts of self defense, when the acts themselves - demolishing 
                  homes, bombarding buildings, blockading whole towns and villages 
                  -- are patently perpetrated to PUNISH WHOLE POPULATIONS, and 
                  I have yet to receive one coherent honest answer from any journalist, 
                  any editor: they are either embarrassingly silent or they react 
                  by promising to be more vigilant next time.<o:p></o:p></font></p>
                <div class="Section1">
                  <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Well, 
                    this has been more than a year that we have been asking for 
                    improvement, or at least for an explanation as to why Israeli 
                    actions are always described as acts of self-defense, and 
                    to date, and nothing has transpired.<o:p></o:p></font></p>
                  <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">And 
                    what is fascinating is that when Palestinians react, their 
                    acts are almost NEVER described as "retaliations" 
                    -- even when the perpetrators themselves call their action 
                    a "retaliation" and even when they record a video 
                    in which they link their act specifically to a particular 
                    Israeli action: an assassination, a home demolition, etc. 
                    At best, we are told that the Palestinians acted to exact 
                    "revenge" -- another code word betraying the underlying 
                    racist subtext: Israelis are rational and measured; they "retaliate" 
                    in self-defense. Palestinians are hot-headed and unable to 
                    contain their passions and emotions: they engage in their 
                    usual tribal acts of revenge, in the best bedouin tradition.<o:p></o:p></font></p>
                  <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">SO 
                    -- ENOUGH!<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Enough 
                    of this sloppy journalism. Enough of casting the aggressors 
                    as the victims, again and again, every single day, brainwashing 
                    the American reader, day after day, with the implicit message 
                     sometimes in BOLD HEADLINES  about Israeli retaliations.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; 
                    </span>ENOUGH!<o:p></o:p></font></p>
                  <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Below 
                    is an interface that will shoot off your letter to all the 
                    news outlets out there: AP, Reuters, Knight Ridder, CNN, and 
                    other media outlets.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; </span>Please 
                    make your voice heard and tell them -- ENOUGH! No more lazy 
                    descriptions of Israeli actions as simple "retaliations".<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; 
                    </span>ENOUGH the racist double standards.<span style="mso-spacerun: yes">&nbsp; 
                    </span></font></p>
                  <p class="MsoNormal"><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Please 
                    mobilize and ask your friends to join in a campaign to shake 
                    the media out of its comfortable trance. </font>F<font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">ill 
                    your personal information, add your comments, and then click 
                    send. </font></p>
                </div>
                <p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="3">Ahmed 
                  Bouzid <br>
                  President<br>
                  Palestine Media Watch <a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/index.html" class="dead" aria-disabled="true"><br>
                  http://www.pmwatch.org</a></font></p>
              </td>
